{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/447674-the-crunch-side-of-ephemeral","id":447674,"title":"The crunch side of ephemeral","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T07:49:14-07:00","id":447674,"title":"The crunch side of ephemeral","content":"I've got a couple questions about spirits and dice pools for people who have played these sorts of things out.<br /> <br /> To begin with, Spirits and the like just have the three Attributes, which are supposed to stand in for the Attribute + Skill that corporeal beings have. That much seems pretty straightforward and clear. The blurb to generally call out what they roll (p. 184) says &quot;They roll the appropriate Attribute + Rank for actions relating directly to their concept, or Attribute + Attribute for actions like surprise or perception&quot;. That seems to suggest that surprise and perception are exceptions to the just-roll-one-Attribute rule and that Rank is a bonus for things particularly in line with the concept. As such, a murder or stealth spirit might roll Finesse + Rank to tail someone.<br /> <br /> All the rolls that specifically say what to roll, though, have something like Power + Finesse, or generally Attribute + Attribute, as though that were the norm. Given the general paradigm of corporeal beings doing Attribute + Skill, that makes sense, but being as each spirit Attribute is supposed to be an Attribute + Skill pool all rolled up, putting two together gets to be pretty intense once you get past Rank 2.<br /> At the bottom edge of Rank 3, a spirit with balanced attributes would have no dice pool below 10, whereas one that stacked a particular stat or pair (and grown naturally from a Rank 2 spirit) would have a minimum of 7 dice for anything at all that they did. At the high end of 3, no pool would be less than 16 dice.<br /> And that's before the stat-boosting that spirits are allowed to do by spending essence.<br /> <br /> So the actual questions I have are these: <br /> Why are so many things that get called out based on two Attributes instead of one?<br /> How do you actually make any headway against anything stronger than a Hursah?<br /> Is the intention that, while Rank 6+ are explicitly untouchable, Rank 4 is roughly the threshold for grand-story-arc-to-overcome?<br /> My best guess as to how to deal with an Ensah that needs to go down is to use Bottle Spirit and then make it into a Fettish, thereby skipping over its defenses entirely. (Sure, the bottling half is risky as the thing gets four turns to kill me or the bottle, but still...)<br /> <br /> What are other ways to deal with actively antagonistic ephemeral beings of higher but approachable ranks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:11:26-07:00","id":447715,"title":"","content":"If at Rank 6+ they become veritable stat-less gods, then it follows that the average spirit at Rank 3 is &quot;dangerous&quot;, at Rank 4 is &quot;very dangerous&quot;, and at Rank 5 is &quot;fucking terrifying&quot;. This is, I'm pretty sure, completely on purpose. It's not a bug, it's a feature. Rank 4-5 Spirits <i>should</i> be scary even to a semi-experienced pack of werewolves. It's the highest tier of &quot;statted&quot; spirits you can get.<br /> <br /> The best way to deal with any spirit, of any Rank, is to decipher its Ban and Bane, and then exploit the ever living fuck out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:46:26-07:00","id":447737,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind the Attribute+Rank is 'for actions relating directly to their concept.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:32:43-07:00","id":447809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/447674-the-crunch-side-of-ephemeral?p=447737#post447737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind the Attribute+Rank is 'for actions relating directly to their concept.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my reason for calling that out, and perhaps I should have stated this explicitly, is that from mid-grade Rank 3 spirit up, you will never have an Attribute that's less than your Rank. As such, all those many, many rolls that are Attribute + Attribute will be stronger than &quot;actions relating directly to their [spirit] concept&quot;.<br /> Thinking about it, it seems plausible that that particular mechanical artifact is a feature and not a bug as it shows that as spirits grow in power, they become less tied to their core concept and more focused on becoming bigger spirits. Or was that not the idea?<br /> <br /> To reiterate one of my first questions, though, does anyone have a story of a time their Storyteller threw a big spirit at them and they managed to deal with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:38:32-07:00","id":447812,"title":"","content":"Looking again at my spreadsheet o' possible spirit stat breakdowns, I see that a spirit who grows with balanced Attributes leaves Rank behind all of it's stats when it stops being the weakest spirit possible. <br /> If a balanced set of stats is your goal, then a Totem made with the minimal 5 dots total has Rank 1 and one Attribute at 1. When your pack collectively gets a sixth dot, its lowest stat bumps to 2 and never again is one of its Attributes at or below its Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:41:19-07:00","id":447838,"title":"","content":"I think pretty much all the rolls you're referencing are either combat (which understandbly uses a different system) or Numina/Manifestation activations. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:43:24-07:00","id":447842,"title":"","content":"If you notice, most of the attribute/attribute stuff is for using their magic. Except that one time where it's cited as what they roll to attack, but that might actually have been a mistake because Dave Brookshaw mentioned in another thread that he meant it to be power + rank even for when a violence spirit throws a punch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:17:39-07:00","id":447899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/447674-the-crunch-side-of-ephemeral?p=447842#post447842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you notice, most of the attribute/attribute stuff is for using their magic. Except that one time where it's cited as what they roll to attack, but that might actually have been a mistake because Dave Brookshaw mentioned in another thread that he meant it to be power + rank even for when a violence spirit throws a punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a lot of the Attribute + Attribute stuff seems to be hold-overs from 1E.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned it in the Errata thread, and I hope it gets fixed. A confusion, that deep, this early could cause confusion for the entire rest of the edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:32:39-07:00","id":447932,"title":"","content":"I went though the book with a search. Here's what I found for multiple-attribute rolls:<br /> <br /> Seeing through an Ithaeur's 4-dot moon gift takes Finesse + Resistance penalized by a Rank, though not the viewers (117)<br /> Attempts to steal Essence are Power + Finesse contested by Power + Resistance (184)<br /> Gorging on Essence at a point of suitable Condition is Power + Finesse (184)<br /> Voluntarily coming into contact with bane takes Resolve + Composure (185)<br /> Attacking is listed as Power + Finesse (185 &amp; 186) <br /> Using and influence requires Power + Finesse (186)<br /> Power + Finesse to read an Urged beings thoughts or urge it to act (190)<br /> Detaching from a Claimed host is Power + Finesse - Rank (191)<br /> Each Numina is activated by a Power + Finesse roll (191)<br /> The Implant Mission Numina calls for a special Power + Finesse roll, possibly redundant with the previous line (192)<br /> The idigam Essence Trap power uses a Power + Finesse roll, opposed by just Resistance (217)<br /> Idigam powers of Gauntlet, Ghost, and Spirit Manipulation all call for Power + Finesse rolls, with the latter two being opposed by Finesse + Resistance (218)<br /> Several other idigam powers, including all of the Forge Servant ones...<br /> Also, Totems oppose the Totem's Wrath (Honor Facet of Gift of the Pack) with all three attributes combined.<br /> <br /> So most of those do seem like the use of powers, other than the attacking one and the seeing through the Spirit Masquerade one. The seeing through the Ithaeur's mask roll seems like you'd almost never be able to fool even a beefy Rank 2 spirit if you slipped up.<br /> That said, what's a spirit ever going to roll for other than to use its powers or to attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:36:09-07:00","id":447940,"title":"","content":"Anything os a social or mental nature, likely. Negotiation, that sort of thing. Negotiating with a Spirit of Arguments or a Spirit of Negotiation or a Spirit of Deals would probably be Finesse + Rank on part of the spirit, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:38:03-07:00","id":447942,"title":"","content":"Social rolls vs werewolves?<br /> <br /> 'sup, ninja?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-18-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:42:31-07:00","id":447944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/447674-the-crunch-side-of-ephemeral?p=447899#post447899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, a lot of the Attribute + Attribute stuff seems to be hold-overs from 1E.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned it in the Errata thread, and I hope it gets fixed. A confusion, that deep, this early could cause confusion for the entire rest of the edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, I don't know, the God-Machine chronicle mentions that ephemeral creatures use Power+ Finesse to attack too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:00:19-07:00","id":447961,"title":"","content":"Maybe that's an exception brought about by self preservation being a sort of universal thing. Gives some of the low power nimble types some bite in a fight because they'll not have the defense of a material being with equivalent wits/dex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:29:56-07:00","id":447990,"title":"","content":"When my search brought up idigam using Power + Finesse for stuff, I thought to check on their slated Ranks for points of reference.<br /> The Idigam Chronical fictions (meant to give a taste for this game) presented them as nigh-unkillable super-spirits that you have almost no hope of ever dealing with.<br /> The Prey chapter in WtF2e has several examples of idigam being Rank 4...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:32:15-07:00","id":447994,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty certain it is supposed to be Power + Finesse to attack, given those rules have been repeated across all the 2e rulesets that feature ephemeral entities so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:41:56-07:00","id":448004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/447674-the-crunch-side-of-ephemeral?p=447990#post447990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W<br /> The Prey chapter in WtF2e has several examples of idigam being Rank 4...</div> </div> </div> </div>A rank 4 idigam would kick the ass of any rank 4 spirit. Have you actually looked at what they can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:42:44-07:00","id":448005,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry, it was my mistake in that post, not in the book. I forgot they treat combat rolls differently to other &quot;skills&quot; when making up the example for the post.<br /> <br /> Spirit Ranks are not supposed to map to Primal Urge levels in any sort of D&amp;Dish &quot;challenge level&quot;. A Rank 1 or 2 Spirit is a pushover for a pack, a Rank 3 one is a challenge. A Rank 4 one is a serious challenge, and a Rank 5 one a major antagonist even a werewolf will have a hard time with. After that, Spirits are firmly into &quot;you don't need stats for these&quot; - Luna herself is Rank 8, and the Tribal Totems Rank 7. But we did import the notion from Mage that godlike Spirits can make Rank 5 avatars when they want to talk to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:37:01-07:00","id":448043,"title":"","content":"So Rank 5 is similar to Ochemata from Mage, which, if I remember from the end of Soul Cage, took an army with several very beefy mages in it to bring down when you actually played it out.<br /> Okay. Well, its good to know where they fit into the stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 03-18-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}